module domicile.mojom;

// THROWAWAY. Step 3's proof, and nothing else.
//
// The producer knows what colour it submitted. What it cannot see is what the
// display compositor drew, and that is the only thing worth knowing: whether
// viz aggregated a frame from a process that is not a renderer into a page's
// layer tree, because a <canvas> in that page named its SurfaceId.
//
// Step 2 asked the same question of a ui::LayerSurface in the browser's own
// window, and answered it with a CopyOutputRequest on that layer. There is no
// such layer any more — the embedding one belongs to the page — so the copy is
// of the browser's window, and the page puts the canvas where the sample lands.
//
// Deleted when domicile-compositor submits real buffers and the measurement in
// ENGINE-FORK.md's step 4 replaces this with something that reads CSS.
interface SpikeProbe {
  // Copies what the display compositor drew for the browser's window and
  // returns the colour at its centre, as SkColor (ARGB).
  //
  // Fails if there is no window yet, or nothing has been drawn — retry.
  SampleWindowCenter() => (bool sampled, uint32 argb);
};
